{"seconds": 55.5, "exit": 0, "final": "After Qxc3, White can play Bxh8, but Black is up a full knight (3 points). This is winning for Black. Let me verify the complete line once more by going back to the initial position and checking Qb4 as the best move:\n\nThe line is: **Qb4 Bxf6 Qxb2 Bxg7 Qxc3**\n\nThis wins material for Black\u2014a net of +3 (knight) after the exchanges.\n\n**Best move:** Qb4\n\n**Main line:** Qb4 Bxf6 Qxb2 Bxg7 Qxc3\n\n**Motif:** fork (the queen on b2 forks the rook on a1 and knight on c3; after Bxg7 Qxc3 wins the knight)\n\n**Coaching note:**\nWhen your opponent attacks your bishop, look for active queen moves that create multiple threats. Here, Qb4 centralizes your queen to attack the b2 pawn and c3 knight simultaneously. After White takes your bishop anyway (Bxf6), you capture b2 with check-like threats, and when White attacks your g7-pawn, your queen snaps up the undefended knight for a decisive material advantage. The key: **active pieces create tactics**.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qb4\", \"line\": [\"Qb4\", \"Bxf6\", \"Qxb2\", \"Bxg7\", \"Qxc3\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10", "move": "Qxc3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10", "move": "Ng4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "rn2k2r/pp2bppp/2p1pn2/q5Bb/3P4/2N2N1P/PPP1BPP1/R2QR1K1 b kq - 1 10", "move": "Ne4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_mov